{title: The First Noel}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}

The [G]first No[D]el the [C]angel did [G]say,
Was to [C]certain poor [Bm]shepherds in [C]fields as [D]they [G]lay;
In [G]fields where [D]they lay [C]keeping their [G]sheep,
On a [C]cold winter's [Bm]night that [C]was [D]so [G]deep.

{label: Chorus}
[G]Noel, [D]Noel, [C]Noel, [G]Noel,
[C]Born is the [Bm]King of [C]Is[D]ra[G]el.

They [G]looked [D]up and [C]saw a [G]star,
Shining [C]in the [Bm]east, be[C]yond [D]them [G]far;
And [G]to the [D]earth it [C]gave great [G]light,
And [C]so it con[Bm]tinued both [C]day [D]and [G]night.

{label: Chorus}
[G]Noel, [D]Noel, [C]Noel, [G]Noel,
[C]Born is the [Bm]King of [C]Is[D]ra[G]el.

And [G]by the [D]light of [C]that same [G]star,
Three [C]wise men [Bm]came from [C]coun[D]try [G]far;
To [G]seek for a [D]king was [C]their in[G]tent,
And to [C]follow the [Bm]star wher[C]ever [D]it [G]went.

{label: Chorus}
[G]Noel, [D]Noel, [C]Noel, [G]Noel,
[C]Born is the [Bm]King of [C]Is[D]ra[G]el.
